==================== Input ====================
# Bail-out 5 of 5: a block scalar whose output depends on its position.
#
# `write_block_scalar` decides whether it owns its trailing newlines by comparing its span end
# against the stream's last descendant, and the final newline of the file is decided from
# whether the stream's last descendant is keep-chomped. Both read source order, so neither
# follows an entry to a new position: moving one emits a trailing blank line at EOF or loses
# the file's final newline, and re-formatting that output would change it again.
#
# `/safe` is the case that must not be refused: a folded scalar with a single trailing newline
# is position-independent, and this shape is pervasive in real specs (`description: >-`).
openapi: 3.0.0
paths:
  /blank-tail:
    get:
      responses: {}
      description: |
        literal text

      operationId: op
  /keep-chomped:
    get:
      responses: {}
      description: |+
        kept text
      operationId: op
  /safe:
    get:
      responses: {}
      description: >-
        folded text that is safe to move
      operationId: op

